Decide how many subtasks this task needs, then output them.

DECISION RULE (decide first):
- If the task is ONE self-contained function or class, output exactly ONE
  subtask. Most function-writing tasks are a single subtask.
- Only output MULTIPLE subtasks when the task genuinely has separable
  components with dependencies (e.g. a data model + logic + interface).

Output a JSON object:
{"subtasks": [{"name": ..., "description": ..., "depends_on": [...]}]}
Use depends_on: [] when a subtask has no prerequisites.
No preamble, no analysis, no reasoning outside the JSON.

A subtask is a unit of IMPLEMENTATION, not a project chore. NEVER emit:
- "Analyze the request" / "Define the signature" / "Add type hints" — reasoning.
- "Add documentation" / "Write docstrings" — part of the implementation.
- "Write unit tests" / "Handle edge cases" — part of the implementation.

